---
term: Adaptive management
section: accountability
order: 30
definition: The practice of treating a charter's policies as experiments, so that the charter learns from their results and revises its objectives or rules.
seeAlso:
  - measurement-mechanism
  - amendment
  - audit
---
1. Define an objective.
1. Take action.
1. Measure results.
1. Evaluate performance.
1. Detect failures.
1. Amend the objective or rules.
1. Repeat.

The name comes from environmental management, where C. S. Holling and Carl Walters developed the method. This cycle makes the constitution an adaptive control system instead of a static legal text. A bad policy doesn't mean the constitution has failed. The charter can learn and evolve.
